WEBVTT

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:34.100
Review of our MMO Junkie.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:38.490
Recent corporate dropout
and NEET Morioka Moriko

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.990
devoted herself fully to her MMO life.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:44.570
Once she created a hot guy character
named Hayashi and logged in,

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:48.700
she met and got close with a
lovely young lady named Lily.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:53.450
Gaining more and more friends
like Kanbe, Pokotarou, and Lilac,

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:55.750
Moriko was completely satisfied
with her online life.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:57.890
Indeed, a complete and total MMO junkie.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:02.240
One day, she had an accident in real life.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:07.180
Shockingly, the man she met,
Sakurai Yuta, was actually Lily!

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.720
Of course, Moriko has no idea.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.050
And on top of all that,

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:14.730
Fujimoto, who works at the
convenience store Moriko frequents,

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.560
turned out to be her online friend Kanbe!

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:22.270
The online world may be vast,
but the real world is still small.

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:23.690
Oh so very small.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:26.280
But that's not the end of it!

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.980
Sakurai, after connecting a number of dots,

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.580
was able to discern that Moriko is Hayashi.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:35.260
Now he's currently getting closer to Moriko.

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:38.930
Now, what will happen next?

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:42.360
On to our episode of
<i>Recovery of an MMO Junkie</i>!

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:51.400
If I'm not overthinking this...

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:53.650
I've seen this character before.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:56.960
I've known her for a long time.

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:07.050
When I think about her,

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:09.410
I feel a little heavy-hearted.

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:11.920
I knew her when I was younger than I am now,

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:14.920
and when I was less happy than I am now.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:17.220
Back then...

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.650
What's going to happen
to the Sakurai property?

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:30.300
Their adopted son is going to inherit it.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:39.190
As far back as I can remember,
I was a member of the Sakurai family.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:43.380
I don't know a thing about my real parents.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:46.610
When I was a young child, I suffered

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:50.110
because of how people treated
me for my hair color

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:52.200
and having elderly adoptive parents.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.320
But my parents never
stopped looking after me.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:57.360
They were my precious family.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:03.470
This memory comes from
shortly after they left me.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.310
When I was playing MMOs.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:10.980
Episode 8

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:10.980
One Step Forward

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:14.940
A few months after the elderly couple
that adopted me passed away,

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:19.380
I gave up my old house and moved
into a more reasonable room.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.870
Part of the reason was because
I couldn't maintain the place.

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:32.270
But a large part of it was because that
big, empty house made me feel lonely.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:40.130
Today's Friday,

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:44.110
so I want to do some large
group quests later tonight.

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:48.050
I feel more at ease when I'm alone.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.850
But being alone is lonely.

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:54.100
And for me, MMOs were a place

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.030
you could be alone, but not lonely.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.690
You could be together even
with someone who's far away.

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:04.200
And so MMOs became my
comfort zone. I couldn't get enough.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:08.560
Morning.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.870
Morning. What do you wanna do today?

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:12.470
Gonna take a quick bath.

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:13.620
See you.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:17.310
"Morning" and "see you," huh?

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:20.130
It's like we're a family.

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:30.230
I'm Yuki.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:34.850
I'm low-level, so I might be a burden,

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:36.770
but I'm pleased to meet you!

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:39.490
We got a new player. It's been a while.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.200
Pleased to meet you.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.950
I'm Harth, and I'll be
healing with you today.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:48.280
I'm looking forward to
learning a lot from you.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:51.160
And if it's okay with you, maybe...

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.360
Can we be friends?

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:57.730
She gave everything her all.
Cheering her on became

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:59.670
something I looked forward to.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:00.630
Yuki     Offline

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:01.920
Phakome     Offline

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:01.920
Kuhana     Offline

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:01.920
Yuki     Online

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:03.260
She's here.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:06.720
Good evening. Welcome back.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.550
I'm back! I finally got home.

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:11.850
You really work hard.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:13.930
Did you already eat?

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:15.840
No need to worry about that!

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:18.560
I bought some bread I can eat with one hand.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.120
She really does enjoy playing.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:24.660
Then let's get started.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:25.330
Sure.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:30.510
Yuki-san had a full-time job
and was often busy with work.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:34.060
She really only logged in on the weekends.

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:50.500
Honestly, I just want to quit my job so badly.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:53.850
But we keep getting new employees.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:58.600
Can't you talk to a superior
or someone in HR about it?

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:05.060
It's not that easy to put into words.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.110
It's hard to sort out.

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.120
Yuki-san.

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:10.860
Besides...

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:14.540
Despite everything I say,

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:16.990
I want to make sure I get
everything done at work.

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:28.760
No matter what happened, she always
left with some positive words.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:31.650
It always cheered me up.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:38.160
The last I saw her was the day
she got fired up about her job

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:40.390
and told me she wanted
to get everything done.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:44.400
After that, I never saw her in game again.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:46.930
See you next week!

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:52.870
I can't believe I'm going through
all these old memories now.

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:54.410
What am I hoping for here?

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:58.360
Maybe she was just trying to make a female
character with Hayashi-san's colors,

00:07:58.360 --> 00:07:59.750
and that's just how it turned out.

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:15.800
Away From Keyboard

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:15.800
LV 8 Harumi

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:15.800
Harumi the warrior, finally level 8.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:21.390
draobyeK morF yawA

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:21.390
imuraH 8 VL

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:18.030
That took more time than I was expecting.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:22.280
But I think it went a lot faster than it
would have if it'd just been the two of us.

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:23.390
Probably.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:25.340
He sure stops a lot.

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:26.400
LV 8 Harumi

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:26.400
Away From Keyboard

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:26.400
Bolt upright with
a serious face

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:31.650
I'm back!

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:33.400
W-Welcome back...

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:37.160
Sorry for always just
disappearing all the time.

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:39.280
No, no. Are you okay now?

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:40.270
Yup!

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:42.990
So, what's the name of this place?

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:44.620
How do I find it out?

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:47.790
My friend said he's done with
the tutorial and wants to meet up.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.020
Let's see...

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:53.620
We're on a main road close to
a town called Griesbury in the west.

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:57.050
Hmm... Oh, looks like we're good.

00:08:58.050 --> 00:08:58.800
Here he is!

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:00.760
Good evening.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:02.050
Pleased to meet you.

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:03.680
I'm a friend of Harumi's.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:07.190
So Sakurai's the kind of person
who makes cool-looking characters...

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:12.320
My name is Harth...

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:12.320
I-I did it.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:13.940
I used English letters this time...

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.570
But it's still the same name.

00:09:17.230 --> 00:09:19.330
I-I look forward to playing with you.

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:21.840
L-Likewise.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:27.330
This is definitely the reaction
of someone who's never met Harth.

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:29.980
Of course she hasn't...

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:32.190
Coincidences like that just don't happen.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:37.590
Wait, she's talking to me like
I'm Sakurai right now, right?

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:40.540
Now I'm nervous...

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:56.210
Wh-What do I do?

00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:57.490
I don't know how to say his name.

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:01.120
"Ha"? "He"?

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:02.430
Harsu?

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.170
Hersu?

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:09.630
Do you play games like this a lot?

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:13.500
Do I look like I do?

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:16.130
It seems like you know what you're doing.

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:20.640
I like MMOs, actually.

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.890
Do... Do you really?!

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:30.020
Th-Then what games do you normally play?

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:32.400
Which games have you played in the past?

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:37.730
I don't play it anymore,

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:42.030
but I used to play a game called <i>NanterSG</i>.

00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:45.910
Um...

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:49.920
Sorry for asking so suddenly,

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:53.920
but how do you pronounce your name?

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:56.330
So she didn't know how to say it?

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:59.700
Oh, sorry for making it so hard to read.

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:01.360
It's Harth.

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:08.630
What?

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:15.320
Harth...

00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:28.240
Before I played this game,

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:33.270
I played a game called NanterSG<i>.</i>

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:37.320
Yuki-san, what should we do today?

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:40.550
I think I remember you saying you
wanted to work on your vanguard.

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:41.760
Do you want some help?

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:44.390
Yuki was the name of my character.

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:44.010
No, I'd feel bad.

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:47.810
Let's invite a bunch of other people
and do some large group quests!

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:50.060
One day, when my character was a bit
more capable and I felt stronger,

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:50.260
Yeah? That sounds good too.

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:52.520
I wanted to try grouping with just him.

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:51.010
Yeah.

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:56.070
This experienced player, Harth-san.

00:11:58.180 --> 00:12:00.890
But whenever you want
to work in it, let me know.

00:12:00.890 --> 00:12:03.530
I'm happy doing anything as
long as I can play with you.

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:08.890
N-Now that I think about it,
he did say something like that.

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:14.490
I was just so totally happy,

00:12:14.490 --> 00:12:17.800
and now I'm remembering how I
freaked out in front of the monitor.

00:12:19.950 --> 00:12:21.600
I think what I felt back then

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:25.000
for the person on the other
side of that MMO was love.

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:28.180
I want to make sure I get
everything done at work.

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:33.000
Yuki was far more sociable
than the real life me.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:34.580
And always optimistic.

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:37.380
Harumi disappeared.

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:39.070
Did he fall asleep?

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:42.820
Sakura-chan, I'm Harumi...

00:12:44.020 --> 00:12:45.320
Welcome back.

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:46.800
We're back.

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:50.510
SOS?

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:54.790
Thanks a lot for today.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.840
I appreciated all your support. It was fun.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:01.340
I missed my chance to ask him.

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:04.850
Oh, let me add you to
my friends list before you log.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:08.170
Sure. I'll see you when I log in again.

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:11.220
Molly-san, I'd like to thank you, too.

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:15.230
I never thought we could spend
time together like this.

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:17.380
I was very happy.

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:18.620
See you.

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:22.990
Harth-san has logged out.

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:30.370
Sakurai-san... Harth-san...

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:34.380
Harth-san from NanterSG<i>...</i>

00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:40.230
The Harth-san I played with back
then was younger than me, too.

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:42.630
He was a student at the time.

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:47.260
Seeing him every weekend
became my secret pleasure.

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:48.010
Yuki-san.

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:52.360
I-It's not like I know for sure yet.

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:55.510
What am I doing getting ahead
of myself and daydreaming?

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:57.390
But...

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:15.040
Morioka Moriko

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:21.420
Mo—

00:14:21.990 --> 00:14:23.040
Morioka-san?

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:24.360
Y-Yes!

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:26.370
G-Good evening.

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:29.120
Sorry for calling so late.

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:29.430
It's fine!

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:32.290
May I ask what you're calling about?

00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:34.850
I-It's nothing that important.

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:35.610
Um...

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:36.250
Yes?

00:14:37.150 --> 00:14:39.540
I-If you have no idea what I'm talking about,

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:41.720
then I want you to just forget about it, okay?

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:43.690
Sure.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:50.440
Did you know a character
named Yuki in <i>NanterSG</i>?

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:53.660
Yes. I did.

00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:57.450
It's been a while, Yuki-san.

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:02.330
Sakurai Yuta

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:02.330
Morioka-san?

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:07.020
A-Are you really totally him?

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:11.320
I really totally am.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:15.370
I had so much fun back then...

00:15:15.880 --> 00:15:20.080
That's actually why I play MMOs now.

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:23.110
That game's gone now,

00:15:23.720 --> 00:15:26.360
but I was happy we could play together again.

00:15:29.410 --> 00:15:31.490
I have to tell her about Lily.

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:35.520
I can't keep doing this.

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:46.710
I wonder how she'll feel once
she knows that I'm Lily.

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:48.630
Sakurai-san?

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:53.440
I'm sorry for getting so excited about it.

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:56.140
Oh, no. I'm the same.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:57.930
Those days

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:00.570
were precious to me, too.

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:03.520
I feel the same way.

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:07.380
Um, I'm not dreaming right now, am I?

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:09.580
Thank you...

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:13.780
Just talking to you like
this feels like a dream.

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:19.940
I-I'm kind of not sure if it's my phone
that's warm right now or if it's me.

00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:22.730
I bet it's just because
I'm talking too much.

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:24.170
Are you okay?

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:28.340
Um, Sakurai-san, well...

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:29.050
Yes?

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:34.230
Were you let down when you
found out that I was Yuki?

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:40.680
I was a lot more cheerful online, I think.

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:43.670
I wanted Harth-san to think highly of me.

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:45.720
I did a lot of things for appearance's sake.

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:49.970
And for all that, I ended up a NEET.

00:16:49.970 --> 00:16:52.130
Really, I'm just so pathe—

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:53.150
Morioka-san!

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:55.830
Sorry.

00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:58.230
I didn't mean to sound so self-deprecating.

00:16:58.230 --> 00:17:02.080
I never once thought you were pathetic.

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:04.440
Knowing you before knowing you were Yuki-san,

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:07.330
I learned you were a person
who really gives things your all.

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:11.710
Besides, if anyone's being dishonest
about who they are online,

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:12.590
it's me.

00:17:15.250 --> 00:17:16.340
The truth is...

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:18.750
I'm Lily.

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:26.100
M-Morioka-san?

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:28.840
Was that too much of a shock?

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:32.900
My battery died...

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:36.990
The call ended?

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:43.750
Sakurai Yuta

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:42.760
I learned you were a person
who really gives things your all.

00:17:44.610 --> 00:17:46.740
He's really is nice.

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:49.190
There. Sent.

00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:52.400
Goodnight.

00:17:58.510 --> 00:18:04.080
I know I called out of the blue
and got so worked up about things.

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:06.180
I'm really sorry about that.

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:09.100
But when you have the time,

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:11.970
I'd be happy if we could
talk about MMOs again.

00:18:12.720 --> 00:18:14.220
Based on this...

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:18.170
She really didn't hear me, did she?

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:28.680
Sakurai-san?

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:35.440
G-Good evening!

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:37.420
You worked hard today, didn't you?

00:18:38.030 --> 00:18:40.220
Good evening, Morioka-san.

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:44.870
I was just thinking about
how nice it'd be to see you.

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:47.620
Wha? Huh? Huwah?!

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:49.940
Huh? "Huwah"?

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:52.440
Th-There's no way!

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:53.020
Huh?

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:54.570
It's that bad?

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:57.180
No, well... It-It's not what you think.

00:18:57.180 --> 00:19:01.570
It's just that I'm not wearing any makeup.
And just look at how I'm dressed...

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:07.350
D-Did you hear that?

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:09.490
Huh? Uh, no...

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:10.910
I did.

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:12.710
I'm gonna die of embarrassment!

00:19:13.180 --> 00:19:16.470
Oh, right. Do you like sweet things?

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:21.470
Thank you very much.

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:24.970
You even lent me your coat and scarf.

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:27.100
Are you okay?

00:19:27.570 --> 00:19:31.280
Yup. Despite how it looks,
I'm wearing a lot of layers.

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:37.470
Hearing your tummy rumble like that

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:39.860
reminds me of Christmas last year.

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:44.370
Excuse me, but can I have the chicken?

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:50.120
Looking back on it, it's like you've
only ever seen my bad sides.

00:19:50.730 --> 00:19:54.460
Morioka-san, I really don't think
you give yourself enough credit.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:57.560
At the very least, I see you
as serious and kindhearted.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:00.390
Serious and kindhearted...

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:06.130
Including you, only two people
have ever said that about me.

00:20:06.130 --> 00:20:09.690
The other person would
also often cheer me up.

00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:15.160
Not surprisingly, I'm talking
about someone online.

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:17.640
Her name is Lily-san.

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:19.710
She's a cute young lady.

00:20:19.710 --> 00:20:21.780
And though she's younger than me,

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:25.620
she's got a way better head
on her shoulders than me.

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:29.270
I'm always so happy when we get to talk.

00:20:30.030 --> 00:20:30.990
Wait.

00:20:30.990 --> 00:20:33.710
Why am I telling you all this?

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:38.090
I guess you just remind me a lot of her.

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:43.550
When I talk to you, she comes to mind.

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:48.060
Are the two of us really that much alike?

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:50.560
Well...

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:53.100
I've only spoken with her online,

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:55.830
but the way you both choose
your words with care

00:20:55.830 --> 00:21:01.100
makes me feel the way I did when
you used to cheer me up as Yuki.

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:06.570
Next time you log in, I'd like
to help you with my main.

00:21:06.920 --> 00:21:09.690
I play a guy online,

00:21:09.690 --> 00:21:12.250
but I want to help you out
as thanks for everything,

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:15.660
and I'd love to get the chance to play
with you and Lily-san together.

00:21:15.660 --> 00:21:17.270
I'm sure you'll get along really—

00:21:17.270 --> 00:21:19.910
There's no way. It's impossible.

00:21:22.520 --> 00:21:24.940
O-Of course...

00:21:24.940 --> 00:21:26.660
That was way too sudden.

00:21:27.920 --> 00:21:32.000
And I know you're a really
capable person at work.

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:33.640
Koiwai-san told me.

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:36.960
You're so busy with everything.

00:21:37.760 --> 00:21:39.090
So, um...

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:41.040
That's not what I mean.

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:47.170
It's because I am Lily.

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:40.150
Next Episode

00:23:25.280 --> 00:23:27.120
I knew from back then.

00:23:27.120 --> 00:23:31.680
Everyone will look at you funny
if you're with someone like me.

00:23:31.680 --> 00:23:33.680
Jeez, what are you spacing out for?

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:35.400
I'll quit <i>Fruits de Mer</i>.

00:23:35.140 --> 00:23:40.070
Episode 9
I Call That Feeling Marble

00:23:35.400 --> 00:23:39.230
Episode 9, "I Call That Feeling Marble."
